# third_party/ds4 (1bit-MONSTER/ds4 1bit/main) commit the daily bump-ds4 run must not move
# away from. While a commit is named here and it is the engine's pin, bump-ds4 does not
# merge upstream into 1bit/main, opens no PR, and reports "held" as a notice instead of
# failing - so a deliberate hold is not ten days of red runs and issue threads. When the
# hold is lifted (empty this file of its commit line), the next scheduled run merges as
# usual. A sha that is NOT the engine's pin is ignored with a notice: the hold only means
# anything about the pin the engine actually carries.
#
# HOLD: DwarfStar's HIP port is two upstream CUDA entry points behind. Upstream antirez/ds4
# ee7e8405 (merged with a resolved Makefile conflict as fork commit c5b276b, kept in the
# release lane at ~/wt/ds4-lib branch bump-ee7e8405) builds ds4, ds4-server and ds4-bench on
# HIP and passes the bump workflow's own guards, but DS4_TEST=1 scripts/build-ds4.sh fails
# linking tests/test_mxfp4_rocm because ds4_deepseek41_cuda.cuh:796 calls
#   ds4_gpu_attention_output_low_q8_rows_exact_tensor
#   ds4_gpu_matmul_q8_0_kslice_rows_tensor
# and neither exists in the HIP/ROCm layer (ds4_rocm.c, cuda/mmq/*.rocm.c, the
# ds4_ggml_stubs/d2r_stubs pattern) - they came in with upstream's DeepSeek-V4-Flash CUDA
# work (a04f46f, 77570b4, 43a91aa). Owner decision 2026-10-30: hold the pin here rather than
# ship a bump whose own check cannot pass. The queued DwarfStar task is to port or honestly
# stub those two entry points, re-run DS4_TEST=1 on Strix Halo, then merge c5b276b into
# 1bit/main and move this pin. Nothing in the release builds anything from this pin.
